{
  "requirement": "The SDK presents node inputs using the returned value's `NodeContents::format`\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.\nIts text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet contents = domain.node_content(&node_id)?;\nlet text = contents.format();\n```\n\nLoading and fallible preparation occur in `Domain::node_content` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`. For inputs queued on an ask\nbuilder, these failures return `ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node`\ntool call, they are returned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue\nand recover.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation of `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`.\n\n1. **Inputs are presented through the returned value's `format`.**\n   - `agent/tests.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` installs a custom formatter. It asserts that the first user message sent to the agent contains \"formatted input: source\", and that the dependency fingerprint comes from the same read.\n   - `tests/validation.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` asserts the formatted inputs in the agent request, in order and with repeats, along with the matching read order and dependencies.\n   - `agent/tests.rs#fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]` asserts the domain-supplied contents in the agent message, in order.\n   - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` asserts that `format` uses the supplied, already-read contents.\n\n2. **Text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation, and formatting needs no further reads.**\n   - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` changes the underlying data after the read. It then asserts `format()` still returns \"before\", the fingerprint equals the snapshot fingerprint, and `reads` is still `[1]`.\n\n3. **Failures on queued ask-builder inputs return `ValidationError::Graph`.**\n   - `tests/validation.rs#fn[queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation]` covers a loading failure (`fail_read`) and a preparation/rendering failure (`fail_prepare`). Both give `Err(ValidationError::Graph(..))`. It also asserts that no dependency is recorded and that no agent request is made.\n   - `tests/validation.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` adds the no-agent case.\n\n4. **Failures during a `read_node` tool call go back to the agent as a tool error so it can recover.**\n   - `agent/tests.rs#fn[node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents]` makes `Domain::node_content` fail during a `read_node` call. It asserts that the next request carries a `ToolResult` with `is_error` set, tool name `read_node` and the error text. It also asserts that the agent then submits successfully and that no dependency is recorded.\n   - This test exercises a preparation failure. A loading failure inside `read_node` uses the same `Domain::node_content` error path, and the requirement describes both under one clause. Loading failures are tested on the queued path.\n\nI found no plausible violating behavior that these tests would accept, and I found no acknowledged gaps.",
  "references": "e7f4eb67f320fdbe3324029052cd29b2da4b151db0ea7c22bb85c62a7c32b9ac",
